++# MVSTATE-REUSE1 selector-to-repair state handoff specification
++
++## Status
++
++Planned after CAMPAIGN-PERF-QUAL1 / architecture revision 102.
++
++## Purpose
++
++Remove duplicated exact sparse-state reconstruction between MVSEL1 and REPAIR1 without changing selector rank authority, target sizes, repair objective/tie semantics, accepted/rejected swaps, or final qualification authority.
++
++## Required realization
++
++MVSEL1 SHALL be able to emit an authenticated reconstructible `TargetMultiViewSelectionStateCache` (name may be refined during implementation) that contains enough terminal sparse execution state for REPAIR1 to begin from the exact selected master order without replaying thousands of `_select_and_update` operations. Its identity MUST bind the MVIDX authority, ordered selection/master-order digest, selector policy identity, and sparse-kernel schema, while excluding worker count, queue depth, storage location, and other execution knobs.
++
++REPAIR1 SHALL authenticate the state cache before use. Missing, stale, incompatible, or corrupt cache state MUST rebuild through the existing exact selector-state replay rather than silently weaken authority. The old replay path remains an exact oracle for qualification.
++
++For smaller repair rungs derived from the master order, the implementation MAY use exact inverse/deselection updates or cached checkpoints if byte/state equivalence is proven after every required rung. It MUST NOT alter rank decisions or repair inputs.
++
++A repair proposal executor MAY be retained/reused across iterations if profiling confirms a gain; task completion order remains non-authoritative and winner reduction remains canonical.
++
++## Acceptance
++
++Qualification MUST compare:
++
++- every selector state array required by repair, not only final selected IDs;
++- every accepted/rejected repair swap and terminal order;
++- MVQUAL plan/digest after repair;
++- cold rebuild and authenticated restart paths;
++- memory overhead and cumulative target-chain wall time.
++
++The gate is successful only if state handoff removes material duplicated work on the integrated closure fixture without changing any scientific record.
